{"B_expression":"-1/(2*(1+sqrt(1+r))**2)","C_expression":"-1/2","derivation":"Retained from the prior draft (P02_W0). B(r) = -1/(2*(1+sqrt(1+r))^2) is the source-Proposition-7.6 stable-form body: with u=0 it makes the pure remainder 2g+g^2-r vanish exactly for all r in the chi_r support, via the identity r^2/(2(1+sqrt(1+r))^2) = (2+r)/2 - sqrt(1+r). C(r,u) = -1/2 is a constant that cancels the leading ur cross-term in the full residual E = ur + r^2/4 + 2(r^2*B + ur*C) + r(r^2*B + ur*C) + (r^2*B + ur*C)^2: the coefficient of ur becomes 1+2C = 0. Both bodies are smooth on an open neighbourhood of the closed outer rectangle {|r|<=1/2, |u|<=1/4} because 1+r >= 1/2 > 0 throughout, keeping sqrt(1+r) on a positive domain. No new derivation is introduced. The prior program was never applied (active_program was null, reason NO_COMPLETE_PROGRAM on every row), so this submission is the first actual execution of the construction. Numerical expectation: for the UNIFORM rows (|r|~2e-4, |u|~8e-3, well inside both chi supports) the residual should drop from ~1.9e-4 to O(r^2*u + r^3) ~ O(1e-10) or below. For LEFT/RIGHT rows with |u|>=1/4 the chi_u factor kills the correction and z is unchanged, matching the source outer-region behaviour.","inspect":[{"file_id":"CALC/initial.json","limit":4096,"offset":0}],"note":"Program retained unchanged from P02_W0 draft. B is the source-only pure-remainder canceller (exact at u=0, all r in chi_r support); C=-1/2 kills the leading ur cross-term. This is a local two-slot coefficient-field operator within the fixed covariance quotient, not a PDE certificate, not a global NS claim, and not a regrade of the archived R4 finite-root scope. Points with |u|>1/4 (e.g. LEFT x=1/8 s=0 with u=-0.5, or extreme z values like z=17 or z=-3) fall outside chi_u support and receive no correction by design. The analytic smoothness certificate remains NOT_CERTIFIED; the expression is manifestly C-infinity on an open neighbourhood of the rectangle (1+r>0), but finite numeric derivatives do not constitute an all-order certificate. A successor should verify that the first applied update on UNIFORM rows reduces residuals by the expected factor, and that NO_APPLIED_UPDATE persists only for rows outside the chi supports."}